<title>BELGIUM: EU says reviews Mannesmann DBKom deal.</title>
<headline>EU says reviews Mannesmann DBKom deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Monday it was starting a routine probe into a proposal by Mannesmann AG and German railway Deustche Bahn AG to acquire joint control of telecommunications unit DBKom.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the operation apparently fell under the European Union's merger rules which ban creation or strengthening of dominant positions.</p>
<p>The deal was notified to the Commission for clearance on September 20. The Commission has a month from that date to clear it or start a four-month in-depth investigation.</p>
<p>Mannesmann announced earlier this month it had struck a deal with Deustche Bahn for a Mannesmann-led group to buy 49.8 percent of DBKom. The group includes U.S. telecoms giant AT&amp;T and telecoms joint venture Unisource NV.</p>
<p>The operation would create Germany's second-largest phones carrier after Deutsche Telekom. -- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
